{"name":"Amazon Stone","hex":"#7e7873","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amazon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall, strong, athletic woman.","A fairy chess piece which combines the moves of the queen and the knight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amazon"},{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amazonite","blocks":[{"text":"Amazonite, also known as amazonstone, is a green tectosilicate mineral, a variety of the potassium feldspar called microcline. Its chemical formula is KAlSi3O8, which is polymorphic to orthoclase."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Amazonita1.jpeg/330px-Amazonita1.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazonite"},{"title":"Amazon (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Amazon.com, Inc. is an American multinational conglomerate engaged in e-commerce, retail, cloud computing, online advertising, digital streaming, entertainment, and artificial intelligence. Founded in 1994 by Jeff Bezos in Bellevue, Washington, the company started as an online book marketplace that gradually expanded to include virtually all consumer products as well as many other categories, positioned as \"The Everything Store\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg/330px-Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)"},{"title":"Jungle green","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle green is a color that is a rich tone of medium spring green."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Microcline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg/250px-Microcline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Microcline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg/330px-Microcline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Microcline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg/250px-Microcline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMicrocline-Quartz-Albite-48224.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Amazonite%2C_quartz_300-3-7927.JPG/250px-Amazonite%2C_quartz_300-3-7927.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn